⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Stale BOM comment inside `renderInstallers()` contradicts the new write path**

The docstring hunk here now correctly says the `.ps1` entries are BOM-less, but the inline comment on the return map ~90 lines below (`scripts/gen_installers.dart:145-146`) was missed and still describes the **old** behavior:

```dart
    // .ps1 content arrives WITHOUT the BOM; main() adds it at write time
    // (see below) and the golden test asserts the BOM bytes separately.
```

Both halves are now false: `main()` writes `entry.value` verbatim (no BOM added), and the golden test asserts the BOM bytes are **absent** (`isNot([0xEF, 0xBB, 0xBF])`, `test/site/installer_golden_test.dart:83-92`) — the opposite of "asserts the BOM bytes separately". The next maintainer reading the map will conclude the BOM is added downstream and that stripping it in an editor is harmless.

Suggested fix (while the context is fresh):

```dart
    // gh-1945: the .ps1 content is committed BOM-less — the piped
    // `irm | iex` path decodes the served bytes as ISO-8859-1, where a BOM
    // becomes literal `ï»¿` text. The golden test asserts bytes 0-2 are NOT
    // a BOM (see test/site/installer_golden_test.dart).
```

